WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.250
He flooded his own basement the day before the river could.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.730
The whole street is stacking sandbags and he's running a hose into his basement.

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:13.330
His neighbor has three pumps going and yells over flood's not till tomorrow, pal, you're early.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:18.130
But he carries the couch upstairs, shuts off the power, and fills it to the top step.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.780
By dinner, the whole street is calling it the indoor pool.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.260
Then the river comes over the bank and both houses end up in a brown lake.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.360
Next door, the pumps are winning and the neighbor yells,How's the pool??

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.240
But by sunset, there's a crack in the neighbor's wall.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:34.480
Thin as a hair.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.840
By midnight, it's wide enough for a finger and the wall is bending in.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.960
You see, soaked dirt is heavy and it leans on a basement wall like a parked truck.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.040
Ever squeezed an empty soda can.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.690
It crumples a full one won't give.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:54.290
With water inside pushing back just as hard, the indoor pool's walls feel almost nothing.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.320
Flood guides really say to let the water in and not pump until the river drops.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.560
A week later, he drains his pool.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:02.960
Nice and slow.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.680
Off a wet floor and four straight walls.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.470
Next door, the neighbor is pumping his out too.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.610
Except his kitchen is down there with it.
